\Cref{fig:runtime} shows the performance of each of the three variants, along
with \texttt{numpy}'s \texttt{tensordot} for reference (denoted by "np np").

A direct comparison with \texttt{numpy} is not fair, as its implementation is
fully generic and most likely respects IEEE 754 floating point arithmetic.
However, it serves as an interesting comparison with an optimized library, to
show the value of tight implementations in \ac{hpc} projects.

\texttt{numpy} has a significant overhead from function calls, preprocessing to
optimize iteration patterns (such as permuting the order of loops), which is
only amortized for small to medium size tensors.

